{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Who say.</b> They are unclean, and they say to others not to eat the flesh of the swine:" "<b>Draw near to you.</b> Like גשה אליך (approach me):" "<b>For I have sanctified you.</b> Intransitive [verb], like בני יצאוני (Jeremiah 10:20), and likewise it means for I have sanctified myself from you — I am holier than you:" "<b>These.</b> They put smoke in My nose:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:59.912851447Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}